Web frontend (server-rendered Flask/Jinja2 templates + minimal vanilla
JS-free UI) added to the same Flask process as Module 11's API —
src/agro_mirai/api/templates/, src/agro_mirai/api/static/, a new
frontend blueprint (src/agro_mirai/api/routes/frontend.py) registered
additively in app.py. Ran in parallel with Module 13 (Feedback Loop) in
a separate session working the same repo; no conflicts on push.

decisions/0013-frontend-platform-sequencing.md records the locked
platform build order (web now, mobile next, WhatsApp/messaging after)
and the stack choice: same-process Flask templates over a separate
React/Vite SPA, for finishability before Nov 14 and because it means
Module 15 (deploy) provisions one service, not two.

The frontend calls Module 11's own JSON API exclusively — never imports
DecisionEngine or any model class — via src/agro_mirai/api/frontend_client.py,
an in-process helper that issues real request/response round trips
through current_app.test_client() with the server-held API_KEY attached
server-side (never exposed to the browser). Three screens: dashboard
(single-farmer field list, per ADR 0003), field detail (crop
recommendation, irrigation advice, disease-risk alerts, advisories with
severity badges — all pulled from the real GET endpoints, not
recomputed), and an inline feedback form per advisory posting to
POST /feedback (required fields checked against routes/feedback.py's
actual _REQUIRED_KEYS before assuming the shape). "Listen in Kannada"
TTS was not built — no endpoint exposes Explanation.summary_kn or
VoiceService audio today; recorded as a known limitation in the ADR and
on the field-detail page itself, not silently dropped.

15 tests: 8 unit (tests/frontend/test_frontend_unit.py, mocked API
layer) covering _safe_get/_safe_get_list's 404/422-tolerant degradation
and ApiError message extraction; 7 integration
(tests/frontend/test_frontend_integration.py) against a real Flask app,
real DecisionEngine, real crop/irrigation artifacts, and the farm-001
fixture — confirming the dashboard renders, the field-detail page's
rendered advisory titles/ids match what GET /fields/{id}/advisories
actually returns byte-for-byte, an unknown field id renders a 404 error
page (not a 500), the feedback form's POST is retrievable afterward via
DataStore.list_feedback_for_advisory, and invalid ratings are rejected
with the flashed message surfaced in the page. Full suite (excluding
tests/voice/): 177 passed, 0 failed, 19 skipped.

